{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Regular","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L106-L109","doc":"At `q = 1` the classical bracket is `n` — the value the symmetric one only\napproaches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.conventions_never_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.conventions_never_agree","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L92-L104","doc":"**They never agree where both are defined.**  `q - q⁻¹ ≠ 0` already forces\n`q ≠ 1`, and the difference `(1 − q)/q` is then nonzero.  So \"the conventions\ncoincide at `q = 1`\" is a statement about *limits*: at `q = 1` the symmetric\nbracket is `0/0` and has no value to coincide with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm_sub_qClas_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm_sub_qClas_two","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L85-L90","doc":"**The two conventions differ by exactly `(1 − q)/q` at `n = 2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.bridge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.bridge_three","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L75-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.bridge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.bridge_two","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L65-L73","doc":"**The bridge.**  The symmetric bracket at `q` is the classical bracket at\n`q²`, normalised by `q^(n-1)`.  Stated at `n = 2` and `n = 3`, where it is a\none-line field computation; the general `n` statement is the same identity on\ngeometric sums. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm_two","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L56-L63","doc":"`[2]` symmetrically is `(q² + 1)/q` — the form the audit's canonicaliser\nprints, and equal to `q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_two","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L52-L54","doc":"`[2]` classically is `1 + q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_mul_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas_mul_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The classical bracket satisfies its defining quotient wherever `q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qSymm","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The **symmetric** `q`-integer `(qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.QIntegerConventions.qClas","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/QIntegerConventions.lean#L39-L42","doc":"The **classical** (Gaussian) `q`-integer, written as the geometric sum\n`1 + q + ⋯ + qⁿ⁻¹`.  Division-free, so it is total: defined at every `q`,\nincluding `q = 1` where it equals `n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}